# Build output. Regenerable, and large enough to matter on a laptop.
/target
/tools/dev-loop/target

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The kernel half is its own workspace, so its build output is its own directory.
/crates/alo-bounding-kernel/target
/tools/kernel-loop/target

# The kernel-enforcement supervisor's own lock, log, stop flag and the handoffs
# it has already published. Every bit of it is about one machine's run of the
# loop rather than about the repository, and a committed lock file would be a
# lock two checkouts fought over while it meant nothing to either.
/.kernel-loop

# The private half of the image signing key never enters the repository (ADR 0036).
*.key
# **A Keynote presentation ends in `.key` too**, and one is a test fixture this
# repository publishes: `crates/alo-opening` is measured against a real one to
# show that a presentation is **not** called a Pages document. It was swallowed
# silently by the rule above on 2026-09-25 — the test passed on the machine that
# made the file and would have failed on every other — so the exception is
# written here rather than the file being forced in, where the next person
# adding a fixture will see it.
!crates/alo-opening/tests/files/presentation.key
